ct/useRef).\n\n/Users/shakilahmedbillal/Desktop/Main Projact/Xhakil/src/components/charts/use-mount-progress.ts:16:3\n  14 |   const transitionRef = useRef(enterTransition)\n  15 |   // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/refs\n> 16 |   transitionRef.current = enterTransition\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  17 |\n  18 |   useEffect(() => {\n  19 |     progress.set(0)",["3166"],"Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\n/Users/shakilahmedbillal/Desktop/Main Projact/Xhakil/src/components/charts/x-axis.tsx:128:21\n  126 |   const crosshairX = tooltipData ? tooltipData.x + margin.left : null\n  127 |\n> 128 |   const container = containerRef.current\n      |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  129 |   if (!(mounted && container)) {\n  130 |     return null\n  131 |   }",["3167"],"Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\n/Users/shakilahmedbillal/Desktop/Main Projact/Xhakil/src/components/charts/x-axis.tsx:129:9\n  127 |\n  128 |   const container = containerRef.current\n> 129 |   if (!(mounted && container)) {\n      |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  130 |     return null\n  131 |   }\n  132 |\n\nTo initialize a ref only once, check that the ref is null with the pattern `if (ref.current == null) { ref.current = ... }`",["3168"],["3169"],["3170"],"jsx-a11y/alt-text","img elements must have an alt prop, either with meaningful text, or an empty string for decorative images.","JSXOpeningElement",["3171"],"react-hooks/immutability","Error: This value cannot be modified\n\nModifying a value previously passed as an argument to a hook is not allowed. Consider moving the modification before calling the hook.\n\n/Users/shakilahmedbillal/Desktop/Main Projact/Xhakil/src/components/toc.tsx:34:3\n  32 |\n  33 |   // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/immutability\n> 34 |   observer.single = single\n     |   ^^^^^^^^ value cannot be modified\n  35 |\n  36 |   useEffect(() => {\n  37 |     observer.setItems(toc)",["3172"],"better-tailwindcss/enforce-canonical-classes","The classes: \"text-base, leading-none\" can be simplified to \"text-base/none\".",{"range":"3173","text":"3174"},{"range":"3175","text":"3176"},"The classes: \"text-sm, leading-none\" can be simplified to \"text-sm/none\".",{"range":"3177","text":"3178"},{"range":"3179","text":"3176"},["3180","3181"],["3182"],["3183","3184"],["3185"],"react-hooks/rules-of-hooks","React Hook \"React.useRef\" is called conditionally. React Hooks must be called in the exact same order in every component render.","MemberExpression",["3186"],"React Hook \"React.useEffect\" is called conditionally. React Hooks must be called in the exact same order in every component render.",["3187"],["3188","3189"],["3190"],["3191","3192"],["3193"],["3194","3195"],["3196"],["3197"],["3198","3199"],["3200"],{"range":"3201","text":"3174"},{"range":"3202","text":"3176"},"react-hooks/exhaustive-deps","React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'wheel'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.","ArrayExpression",["3203"],["3204"],"React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'hold'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["3205"],["3206"],"React Hook useLayoutEffect has missing dependencies: 'restoredScrollTop' and 'shouldFocus'. Either include them or remove 